<p>Afghan authorities said a Pakistani air strike hit the Omid addiction treatment hospital in Kabul on Monday night, killing at least 400 people and injuring hundreds more as patients ate dinner or rested inside the facility. Witnesses and survivors described fire, collapsing walls, and people trapped in the rubble, while rescue crews kept recovering bodies on Tuesday. Pakistan rejected Afghanistan’s accusation that it targeted a hospital, saying its strikes in eastern Afghanistan aimed at military facilities during a three-week conflict between the two countries. Afghanistan said it would retaliate, raising fears of further escalation, as families gathered at the site searching for missing relatives and rescuers kept working through the debris.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/3GoZ26m8xEqZjaKrHWn-piIVYeDpJY5Qme9FHvUuu-7IdjiMYjSgv2jYv22aQdhRrYx4om4xz2b6xiHb77caNCCLaXthrdksyR-jol-54121ZWciY8nOY_CzYF4YQwSHt8V7dsc23PX-2LjM15OfomMWhiQMFy8BILMu7UOJZWWYvLvQy5VEOZkAigH7IVHTQT-DIOJrscVy5UD4WM7EW-tlH5ip' alt='The airstrike hit a drug rehabilitation center in Kabul, Afghan officials said.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Deadliest episode: Multiple reports described the Kabul blast as the deadliest single attack of the three-week war between Afghanistan and Pakistan.</li><li>Witness detail: Survivors said some victims burned in their beds, while others were crushed by collapsing walls after the strike tore through the building.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pakistan government: Pakistan’s information minister strongly rejected the claim that Pakistan struck a Kabul hospital, and officials said Monday’s operations targeted military facilities in eastern Afghanistan. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/3/17/pakistan-strongly-rejects-claim-it-struck-kabul-hospital'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Afghan authorities: Afghan officials accused Pakistan of bombing the Omid addiction treatment hospital and said the strike hit civilians receiving treatment. (<a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/17/nx-s1-5750477/afghanistan-says-at-least-400-people-are-dead-in-kabul-after-pakistan-airstrike'>NPR</a>)</li><li>Families of victims: Relatives gathered at the ruined hospital to search for missing loved ones, underscoring the uncertainty over who survived and who remained under the debris. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/3/17/families-search-for-loved-ones-after-deadly-attack-on-kabul-hospital'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/17/witness-horrific-scenes-pakistan-air-strike-kabul-drug-rehab-centre'>‘Everything was burning, people were burning’: witnesses describe strike on Kabul drug rehab centre</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ckg1kgz6wkgo'>Air strike hit Kabul rehab centre as patients ate dinner, survivor tells BBC</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/rescue-crews-dig-bodies-from-ruins-of-kabul-hospital-hit-by-airstrike-blamed-on-pakistan'>Rescue crews dig bodies from ruins of Kabul hospital hit by airstrike blamed on Pakistan</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/3/17/pakistan-strongly-rejects-claim-it-struck-kabul-hospital'>Pakistan ‘strongly’ rejects claim it struck Kabul hospital</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/17/nx-s1-5750477/afghanistan-says-at-least-400-people-are-dead-in-kabul-after-pakistan-airstrike'>Afghanistan says at least 400 people are dead in Kabul after Pakistan airstrike</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kabul-hospital-airstrike-pakistan-afghanistan-conflict-india-response-march-17-2026/article70752886.ece'>India terms Pakistan’s bombing of drug rehab centre in Kabul a ‘barbaric’ act</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/17/world/asia/afghanistan-pakistan-kabul-hospital.html'>Dozens Dead in Pakistani Airst